Based on my review of the phase-071 changes, here are the findings:

```
FINDINGS:
1. [MAJOR] src/repl/mod.rs:3029-3034 — `.dir` on an object instance variable shows "kind: record" and omits methods because it uses the expression text (`code.trim()`) as the object type name. For `.dir c` where `c` is a `Counter` instance, `code.trim()` is `"c"`, not `"Counter"`, so `object_type_members("c")` returns `None`. Methods are only shown when the expression is literally the type name (`.dir Counter`). This is a functional gap not covered by tests (tests only check `.dir Counter`, not `.dir <instance>`).
2. [MAJOR] src/repl/mod.rs:2949-2952 — `.types` skips any binding whose name matches a declared object type (`vm.object_type_members(&binding).is_some()`), even if the binding has been rebound to a different shape. Rebinding `Counter` to `{other: 1}` hides the actual shape; the object type's original shape is shown instead. No test covers rebinding an object type name.
3. [MAJOR] src/repl/mod.rs:2985-2995 — `.typehints` shows imported module names (e.g., `files` bound to `Value::Nothing` after `import files`) as `files: nothing` because it uses `session_bindings()` without the filter that `.env` uses (which excludes imported names with `Nothing` value). This leaks internal bindings into the user-facing type hints listing.
4. [MINOR] src/repl/mod.rs:3030-3034 — The heuristic `code.trim()` to recover an object type name from a record value is fragile: it fails for any expression other than a bare type name (e.g., `.dir get_counter()`, `.dir foo.bar`, `.dir c`). The comment acknowledges this but the command semantics suggest it should work on values, not just type names.
5. [STYLE] src/repl/mod.rs:874-893 — `collect_shape_labels` uses the field-only label as the `BTreeMap` key but stores a rendered value that includes methods. Two objects with identical fields but different methods would deduplicate to the first one's method list. Unlikely in practice (methods are part of the type) but the key should include methods for correctness.

REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS 5
```
